### Step 1.7: Student Views Their Application
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications/YOUR_APPLICATION_ID
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_STUDENT_TOKEN

### Step 1.8: Student Views Their Documents
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents?application_id=YOUR_APPLICATION_ID
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_STUDENT_TOKEN

### Step 1.9: Admin Reviews Application
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications/query?status=en_attente
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN

### Step 1.10: Admin Approves Application
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/applications/YOUR_APPLICATION_ID/change_status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN

{
  "status": "approuvee",
  "feedback": "Application approved after thorough review. Congratulations!"
}

### Step 1.11: Student Checks Updated Application Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications/YOUR_APPLICATION_ID
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_STUDENT_TOKEN

### WORKFLOW 2: Encadrant Managing Students

### Step 2.1: Admin Creates Encadrant User
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN

{
  "email": "integration.encadrant@example.com",
  "password": "encadrant123456",
  "nom": "Integration",
  "prenom": "Encadrant",
  "role": "encadrant"
}

### Step 2.2: Encadrant Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "integration.encadrant@example.com",
  "password": "encadrant123456"
}

# Save encadrant token: YOUR_ENCADRANT_TOKEN

### Step 2.3: Encadrant Creates Student
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ENCADRANT_TOKEN

{
  "email": "encadrant.student@example.com",
  "password": "student123456",
  "nom": "Encadrant",
  "prenom": "CreatedStudent",
  "role": "etudiant"
}

### Step 2.4: Encadrant Views Their Created Users
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/users
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ENCADRANT_TOKEN

### Step 2.5: New Student Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "encadrant.student@example.com",
  "password": "student123456"
}

# Save token: YOUR_NEW_STUDENT_TOKEN

### Step 2.6: New Student Creates PFE Application
POST {{baseUrl}}/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_NEW_STUDENT_TOKEN

{
  "application_type": "pfe",
  "type_specific_data": {
    "title": "Integration Test PFE Project",
    "supervisor_name": "Integration Encadrant",
    "company": "Test University",
    "academic_year": "2024-2025",
    "specialization": "Computer Science - Testing",
    "objectives": "Complete integration testing workflow validation",
    "methodology": "Automated testing and manual verification",
    "expected_outcomes": "Fully validated integration workflow"
  }
}

# Save PFE application ID: YOUR_PFE_APPLICATION_ID

### Step 2.7: Encadrant Reviews Student's Application
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications/query?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ENCADRANT_TOKEN

### Step 2.8: Encadrant Requests Revision
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/applications/YOUR_PFE_APPLICATION_ID/change_status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ENCADRANT_TOKEN

{
  "status": "en_revision",
  "feedback": "Please provide more detailed methodology and timeline for the project."
}

### WORKFLOW 3: Incubation Application Process

### Step 3.1: Admin Creates Incube User
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN

