### WORKFLOW 4: Token Management and Security

### Step 4.1: Verify Access Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-token
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_STUDENT_TOKEN

### Step 4.2: Use Refresh Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "YOUR_REFRESH_TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN"
}

### Step 4.3: Verify New Access Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-token
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_NEW_ACCESS_TOKEN

### WORKFLOW 5: File Download and Storage

### Step 5.1: Get Document Download URL
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/YOUR_DOCUMENT_ID/download
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_STUDENT_TOKEN

### Step 5.2: Download File Through Nginx Storage Proxy
# Use the URL returned from Step 5.1
GET http://localhost:5000/storage/documents/YOUR_FILENAME

### WORKFLOW 6: Admin Overview

### Step 6.1: Admin Views All Applications
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications/query?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN

### Step 6.2: Admin Views All Users
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/users
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN

### Step 6.3: Admin Views All Documents
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/all
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN

### WORKFLOW 7: Error Handling and Edge Cases

### Step 7.1: Attempt Cross-User Access
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications/ANOTHER_USERS_APPLICATION_ID
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_STUDENT_TOKEN

### Step 7.2: Student Attempts Admin Action
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications/query
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_STUDENT_TOKEN

### Step 7.3: Invalid Token Usage
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications
Authorization: Bearer invalid.token.here

### Step 7.4: No Authorization Header
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications

